v1.3.11 (2026-05-28)
--------------------
Fix: SecureNAT status always shown as Stopped in hub NAT/DHCP tab.

Root cause was in the frontend bulk cache, not detection:
- The bulk load (/api/hubs/{hub}/all) cached securenat data without _enabled,
  so loadNatDhcp() always read _enabled=undefined → false → "Stopped"
- Fix: inject _enabled from bulk.status.SecureNATEnabled_bool when building
  the securenat cache entry (data already present, just not wired up)

Also fixed along the way (v1.3.9, v1.3.10):
- Backend: get_securenat was calling non-existent GetHubSecureNATStatus →
  now reads SecureNATEnabled_bool from GetHubStatus
- Backend: vpncmd fallback for GetHubStatus now parses "SecureNAT" field
  (key confirmed from SoftEther source Command.c PsStatusGet)
- Backend: asyncio.gather uses return_exceptions=True so a failing
  GetHubStatus doesn't crash the whole securenat endpoint
